{"deleteContentRange":{"range":{"startIndex":144925,"endIndex":145051,"tabId":"t.l5c18frq5wuo"}}},
{"insertText":{"location":{"index":144924,"tabId":"t.l5c18frq5wuo"},"text":"\nThe improvement that RQ1 asks about is therefore present in ranking performance under frozen transfer, in seven of nine directions against Swin-B and in three of nine against Video Swin-B, with no direction in which SwinFusion++ was significantly worse than either encoder. Within datasets, where all three models were near the ceiling, no improvement was detectable, and under transfer the ranking advantage did not carry over to threshold-dependent performance at the frozen source operating points. Whether the transfer differences are due to TLBG-HCA is examined under RQ4, and the verdict against the Chapter 3 criterion for a strong model is given under RQ6."}},
{"updateParagraphStyle":{"range":{"startIndex":144925,"endIndex":145590,"tabId":"t.l5c18frq5wuo"},"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","alignment":"JUSTIFIED","lineSpacing":200,"indentFirstLine":{"magnitude":36,"unit":"PT"},"spaceAbove":{"magnitude":0,"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"magnitude":0,"unit":"PT"},"keepWithNext":false},"fields":"namedStyleType,alignment,lineSpacing,indentFirstLine,spaceAbove,spaceBelow,keepWithNext"}},
{"updateTextStyle":{"range":{"startIndex":144925,"endIndex":145589,"tabId":"t.l5c18frq5wuo"},"textStyle":{"fontSize":{"magnitude":12,"unit":"PT"}},"fields":"bold,italic,underline,backgroundColor,fontSize"}},
{"updateTextStyle":{"range":{"startIndex":145589,"endIndex":145590,"tabId":"t.l5c18frq5wuo"},"textStyle":{"fontSize":{"magnitude":12,"unit":"PT"}},"fields":"bold,italic,underline,backgroundColor,fontSize"}},
{"insertText":{"location":{"index":144924,"tabId":"t.l5c18frq5wuo"},"text":"\nRelative to the fixed recipe, the BO-selected configuration significantly raised ROC-AUC within FF++ C40 and Celeb-DF v2 (the latter depending on the family grouping) and from FF++ C23 to C40, but significantly lowered it in five other transfer directions, consistent with tighter fitting to each training source. Tuning for source-validation ROC-AUC therefore did not translate into better transfer, in line with the broader finding that gains measured on the training distribution need not carry over to new data (Geirhos et al., 2020). Across the nine transfer directions, the fixed recipe ranked target videos significantly better than the BO-selected configuration in five, worse in one, and no detectably differently in three. These results support the use of the fixed-recipe configuration for the web service’s detectors, because videos submitted to the service generally come from outside the detector’s training benchmark (even the built-in sample clips were never offered to a detector trained on the same dataset; Chapter 3), a setting closer to cross-dataset transfer than to within-dataset testing."}},
